Ally Bonney field notes from the Wilds, 6/30/25
Notes on the first camera trap placed (CT02): The shelter on the first right (Nomad shelter), facing the lakes overlooking the two lakes and the landbridge in between at the bottom of Nomad Hill.It is placed high on the load bearing beam on the front right corner of the shelter (when facing the lakes). A lot of deer were congregating here, so we placed two cameras here facing two different directions.
General: The jotforms were not reliable in all parts of The Wilds, so paper backups were used. There was heavy rain before we set up the traps/monitors, but it subsided and was mostly cloudy/sunny while we were placing the equipment. The fourth camera trap site (near the lake) had a running water pump nearby in the lake, which may cause noise pollution.
